WEBVTT

00:00:00.250 --> 00:00:04.400
HouseCairn plans the upkeep and the work of a home, room by room.

00:00:04.750 --> 00:00:06.400
First, the essentials.

00:00:06.750 --> 00:00:10.900
Today: what is late, what is due today, what is coming. Anyone in the household marks a task done in one tap.

00:00:11.250 --> 00:00:14.900
Each room has its equipment, and each piece of equipment its tasks and photos.

00:00:15.250 --> 00:00:18.900
The calendar shows what is planned; a feed sends it to your usual calendar app.

00:00:19.250 --> 00:00:23.400
The budget follows what is planned, committed and paid, within an envelope for the year.

00:00:23.750 --> 00:00:25.900
Example 1: descaling the espresso machine.

00:00:26.250 --> 00:00:30.400
A Descaling task, three months after the last time, on the espresso machine of the kitchen.

00:00:30.750 --> 00:00:34.900
One water filter at €7.90 each time: €31.60 a year.

00:00:35.250 --> 00:00:38.900
The filter comes from the stock: two in the cupboard.

00:00:39.250 --> 00:00:43.400
The maintenance budget counts the task at €31.60 a year.

00:00:43.750 --> 00:00:46.400
Once it is done, one tap on Done…

00:00:46.750 --> 00:00:51.400
…takes one filter from the stock. One left: it shows as low before it runs out.

00:00:51.750 --> 00:00:53.900
Example 2: redoing the bathroom.

00:00:54.250 --> 00:00:57.900
The project holds its tasks, dated like any other.

00:00:58.250 --> 00:01:03.400
Two plumbers' quotes, side by side. The one at €2,850 is accepted on the plumber's budget line.

00:01:03.750 --> 00:01:06.900
Inspiration links stay with the project.

00:01:07.250 --> 00:01:11.400
Planned €4,200, committed €2,850, paid €480.

00:01:11.750 --> 00:01:16.400
And over the year: the €6,000 envelope against what is planned, committed and paid.

00:01:16.750 --> 00:01:20.400
Free software, self-hosted: housecairn.app
